# Build context of backend/Dockerfile, which is built from the REPOSITORY ROOT (docker-compose.yml, and
# `docker build -f backend/Dockerfile .`). The image needs backend/ and scripts/ and nothing else, so
# everything else is excluded: without this the context is the whole repository - docs, frontend
# node_modules, .git - sent to the builder on every build. The frontend image has its own context
# (frontend/) and its own frontend/.dockerignore; this file does not apply to it.
*
!backend/
!scripts/
# Local junk that must never reach the image.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.env
**/.env.*
